ger buffer, so it is worse still.\n\n**Ordering more or less than ×1.05.**\n- **Candidate 1 (×0.95):** it supplies about 10 % less than mean demand. A missed sale costs 10 for product 0 and 25 for product 1, which is more than the savings on purchases and holding. Net, about 300 worse.\n- **Candidate 3 (×1.15):** stock builds up by about 3 units a day per product. Holding and leftover stock at the end cost well over the shortages it prevents. Several hundred worse.\n\n**Candidate 0 against candidate 7.** Candidate 7 adds 30 units of each product to the first delivery and trims the last orders slightly.\n- The first 10 or so of those extra units pay off, because shortages are very likely early on.\n- Units 20–30 are probably not used up for a long time. They run up 15–20 days of holding and often end the month unsold.\n- My rough estimate is a loss of about 80 for product 0 and 70 for product 1 from the buffer. Trimming the final orders gains back about 70.\n- Net, candidate 7 trails candidate 0 by roughly 80. That gap is small next to the random noise, which is why my confidence is only moderate."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 4796, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 4796}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-27T10:12:44.976Z", "request_id": "req_011CgSZV4gxA68AScEvQJ614"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01R9uByYzenwmko28mvTwK47", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"typ